# The pre-release set: what tools/release.sh step 6b runs (through tools/scenarios/prerelease.sh) for the desks a release
# touches. Short scenarios that were green on their last runs on Tower - no reboot half, no clock change, no let-go, nothing
# marked nightly - all of them together ≈ 27 min on Tower (2026-10-21), the base reset and the Mac-side checks on top.
#
# One a line, in the order they run:   <name>   <desk>[,<desk>…]   <seconds on Tower>
# The desks are the ones whose changes call the scenario (prerelease.sh maps the release's changed files to desks); the
# seconds are only for the estimate --dry prints. A scenario that installs another release (office-in-*) stays last: its
# undo puts the released plugin back, the code under test is gone for whatever would run after it.
# `prerelease.sh --self-test` checks this file: every name a scenario here, none nightly or in reboot halves, the total.

office-smoke-refresh                            office                          15
office-sv-docker-off-bubbles                    office                          35

backup-sh-office-share-exists-first-setup       backup                          15
backup-sh-office-share-missing-first-setup-gate backup                         120
